      "content": "It feels inconsistent because the internet isn't one single, unified path; it's a massive, decentralized network of independent servers. Think of it like a huge, sprawling web where different regional servers have their own local caches. When you change an A record, you're telling these scattered caches, \"Hey, new address!\" but each one has its own schedule for checking for updates. Some servers are quick and eager to check the primary source, while others are slow and stubbornly hold onto the old information, which is the root of the inconsistency.",
